      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `--enable-deterministic-inference` on ROCm, FP8 MoE experts still run through AITER's fused MoE when `--moe-runner-backend` is `auto`. Its configuration depends on the token count, so a token's result depends on the other tokens in its batch: Qwen3-30B-A3B-FP8 in deterministic mode on MI350X gives 19-21 different outputs for 50 identical requests. SGLang's Triton MoE runner uses one fixed configuration in deterministic mode.\n\n**Which models this affects.** FP8 MoE checkpoints on ROCm in deterministic mode (Qwen3-30B-A3B-FP8 tested; other FP8 MoE models take the same runner selection, untested). MXFP4 and MXFP8 experts (gpt-oss, MiniMax-M3) and INT4 weights are unchanged.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `layers/quantization/fp8.py`: `Fp8MoEMethod._deterministic_fp8_experts_on_triton()`; when the runner backend is `auto`, deterministic mode keeps FP8 experts off the AITER runner (the Triton runner is used). MXFP4 / MXFP8 experts, INT4 weights, an explicit `--moe-runner-backend` and normal mode are unchanged.\n- New test `test/registered/unit/layers/quantization/test_fp8_moe_deterministic_runner.py`: the runner choice for deterministic and normal mode, FP4 / MXFP8 / INT4 experts and an explicit backend.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nMI350X (gfx950), ROCm 7.2.4, `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.22-rocm724-mi35x-20261021`, deterministic mode (`--enable-deterministic-inference`) together with the other open MI350X deterministic-mode changes (the same in every run). Checks: `python3 -m sglang.test.test_deterministic` (`single`, `prefix`, `prefix --return-logprob`, `radix_cache`, 50 trials) plus a bitwise batch-size check (the same prompt in batches of 1 to 50, 1,275 responses, token IDs and logprobs compared exactly with the batch-size-1 response). GSM8K through sgl-eval, 1,319 questions, temperature 0.\n\n- Qwen3-30B-A3B-FP8 TP1 with this change alone: every check passes (9 / 9 `Unique samples: 1`, logprobs identical, bitwise 1,275 / 1,275); before: single 19-21 outputs.\n- With the block-FP8 linear change too, no flags: every check passes at TP1 (2 / 2 fresh servers), TP2 (2 / 2) and TP4 (1 / 1). GSM8K 95.38% (TP1), 94.92% (TP2).\n- The unit test passes on MI350X (1 passed, 5 subtests).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nQwen3-30B-A3B-FP8, deterministic mode with both FP8 changes, output throughput 1k in / 1k out: TP2 6,792 tok/s (before, not deterministic: 8,035; normal mode 13,775); TP4 10,537 tok/s (normal 20,683). This is the cost of correct results; normal mode is unchanged.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41020842247](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41020842247)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41020842008](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41020842008)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41020842233](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41020842233)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
